[thin] Specific cosmetic-flute profile exception: these true short chords lie in the authored exterior groove, land or fade. All five interior samples lie in the exact final fluted STL. The shared groove is 4 mm wide, 1.2 mm deep and uses a 5 mm smoothstep fade; current pitch is 5.0073 mm. The corner-coupon and appearance scopes are recorded in cadlib/flute-evidence/README.md. This is a specific exterior-contour allowance, with no 3 mm finished-wall, exact deposition or load-capacity acceptance.
alternatives: Flattening or shallowing changes the retained visible contour. Widening lands changes closed-field spacing. Assess a finish change against the appearance evidence rather than choosing it from a thickness-only cutoff.
