[thin] Specific required partition, with a classifier minimum: each row's 1.445 mm minimum pairs the meter anchor's rib crown (Z344.4) inside the tie band with the slab underside (Z343) past the band's end, a corner pair. The real section in the cluster is the 1.95 mm slab between each zip tie's channel and the flow meter's pocket (Y372.56-374.51 and 413.51-415.46). It is the anchor's 1.7 mm inner end web, which the meter's 7.2 mm collar fixes and which keeps the tie on the collar, plus 0.25 mm of slab; the tie channel is the 18 lb tie's 2.5 mm plus 1.0 mm of room; and the pocket keeps 2.0 mm of axial room because the meter is laid into its plain half-bores with nothing locating it along Y, so the pocket walls, not the slab under the label cover's Ø35 rim, are what it meets.
alternatives: A 3 mm partition needs a positive axial stop holding the meter within about 0.9 mm, e.g. the inner end webs carried over the neck with a lead-in, so the pocket can give up the room; a narrower tie channel or a shifted band thins the collar's end webs.
