[thin] Wrong material-thickness classification: stepped-corner pairs. Each pairs two opposed faces that meet only at the edge of a stepped corner of solid stock: a rib crown with the slab underside past a tie band's end, a rib flank with a pocket wall above it, two pockets' roofs either side of a step, a channel floor with the flank face beside a band's end. A ray along each sample's inward normal crosses 7.9-22.7 mm of material (probe on the current STL).
alternatives: Reject pairs whose sample's inward chord through the material reaches the search. No wall change addresses these readings.
