[ceiling] Unavoidable fitted catch bridges: each face is the bearing face of a catch window in `carb-1`'s capped rib, where the anchor cap's lip bears. Back-top prints ceiling-down, so the face is a 14.6 mm bridge carried by the rib's two 3 mm end webs, 4.0 mm over the slab; the window it roofs is the 1.6 mm pocket the lip enters.
alternatives: A corbel or column under the face fills the window the lip enters. Sloping the face turns the lip's pull into a spread that walks the wing out of the window, and a window open at its ends gives up the end webs the bridge stands on.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-back-top.step
